Subject: [PATCH] msm: kgsl: A510: no RPTR register read when retiring

Patch 0015 made the A510 read RPTR from the register, but the two tracepoints
that retire a command still took that path. They run without the device mutex
and, as the comment there says, with the GPU clocks possibly off. The value only
goes to the trace. In the first boot of LineageOS 20 the GPU worked and this
printed a kgsl_pre_hwaccess WARNING for each of the 6058 commands retired in 50
seconds, and the tablet reset by itself at about 70 seconds with nothing in
pstore. A3xx already passes 0 here: do the same.
---
--- drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_dispatch.c
+++ drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_dispatch.c
@@ -313,9 +313,9 @@
 	/*
 	 * For A3xx we still get the rptr from the CP_RB_RPTR instead of
 	 * rptr scratch out address. At this point GPU clocks turned off.
-	 * So avoid reading GPU register directly for A3xx.
-	 */
-	if (adreno_is_a3xx(ADRENO_DEVICE(device)))
+	 * So avoid reading GPU register directly for A3xx and A510.
+	 */
+	if (adreno_rptr_from_register(ADRENO_DEVICE(device)))
 		trace_adreno_cmdbatch_retired(drawobj, -1, 0, 0, drawctxt->rb,
 				0, 0);
 	else
@@ -2353,9 +2353,9 @@
 	/*
 	 * For A3xx we still get the rptr from the CP_RB_RPTR instead of
 	 * rptr scratch out address. At this point GPU clocks turned off.
-	 * So avoid reading GPU register directly for A3xx.
-	 */
-	if (adreno_is_a3xx(adreno_dev))
+	 * So avoid reading GPU register directly for A3xx and A510.
+	 */
+	if (adreno_rptr_from_register(adreno_dev))
 		trace_adreno_cmdbatch_retired(drawobj,
 			(int) dispatcher->inflight, start, end,
 			ADRENO_DRAWOBJ_RB(drawobj), 0, cmdobj->fault_recovery);
